<title>RUSSIA: Russia mulls 80 mln mark credit from German banks.</title>
<headline>Russia mulls 80 mln mark credit from German banks.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Russian government is considering taking an 80 million mark ($48.7 million) credit from a group of German banks to build fishing vessels in the Caspian Sea, a government spokesman said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>German banks will finance most of the equipment needed to manufacture the ships in Russia, he told a news conference.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520 ($ = 1.641 German Marks)</p>
</text>
